  The Prompt Rewrite Effort\
\
  This is the real work. The 6 new prompts need to be written from scratch. But here's the thing \'97 they'd be\
   shorter than the current prompts because you're asking for simpler output.\
\
  Current quick_wins.py prompt: 136 lines asking for 10 quick wins with matrices, escalation paths,\
  dashboards.\
\
  SMB 03_action_plan.py prompt might be 40-50 lines: "Give me 5 things to do this month. For each: what\
  tool, what it costs, what to type, what you get back. Total budget under $100/month."\
\
  The prompts would encode your expertise directly \'97 your preferences for tools, your knowledge of what\
  works for SMB, your aversion to Make.com. The consulting guides become secondary when the prompt itself is\
   opinionated.\
\
  The Consulting Guides\
\
  With a pure SMB app, you have three options:\
\
  Option 1: Keep the 3 SMB guides, drop the enterprise ones\
  - Use smb-ai-playbook.md, smb-ai-value-playbook.md, ai-implementation-steps-smb.md as the only guides\
  - They're decent and contain useful frameworks (BCG 10-20-70, SMB 80/15/5)\
  - Delete or ignore the enterprise guides (BCG, McKinsey, KPMG, etc.)\
  - The guides would be loaded for specific deliverables via the config, same as now\
\
  Option 2: Drop guides entirely, encode your expertise in the prompts\
  - The prompts themselves become the "guide" \'97 your tool preferences, your cost expectations, your\
  recommendations\
  - This is simpler to maintain and more current (guides get dated, prompts can be updated easily)\
  - But you lose the consulting frameworks and statistics that give the output substance\
\
  Option 3: Hybrid \'97 keep the 3 SMB guides + make the prompts opinionated\
  - Use the SMB guides for frameworks and data points\
  - Make the prompts directive about specific tools, costs, and approaches\
  - This gives you both the structured knowledge from the guides AND your personal expertise in the prompts\
\
  I'd recommend Option 3. The SMB guides are useful for giving Gemini substance (the statistics, the\
  frameworks), while the prompts control the structure and recommendations.\
\
  What About the PPTX/DOCX/PDF Generators?\
\
  These work on whatever content they receive. The pptx_generator.py generates an "Executive Summary Deck"\
  and a "Full Findings Presentation" \'97 for SMB you could simplify these to produce one shorter deck instead\
  of two. But the generators themselves don't need to know anything about SMB vs enterprise. They just\
  format whatever markdown they're given into slides/documents.\
\
  The DOCX/PDF generators are the same \'97 they produce a "Final Strategy Report" from whatever deliverables\
  exist. With 6 SMB deliverables, the report would be shorter and more focused automatically.\
\
  Research Queries\
\
  The current research queries in research/orchestrator.py run 6 phases: company overview,\
  leadership/funding, industry, competitors, tech landscape, regulations. For SMB, you could:\
\
  - Keep as-is \'97 the research still works fine for gathering company context\
  - Simplify \'97 skip the "regulatory context" phase, skip "competitive intelligence" (SMBs don't need Azure\
  vs AWS comparisons)\
  - Add SMB-specific queries \'97 "affordable AI tools for [industry] small businesses," "common pain points\
  for [industry] businesses under 10 employees"\
\
  The research phase is the least problematic part. It's generic enough to work for any company.\
